{"units": [{"id": "zoma-def1", "translation": "girdle (a kind of tunic)"}, {"id": "zoma-note1", "translation": "See πεζοφόρος."}, {"id": "zoma-quote1", "translation": "with girdles that reach the feet"}, {"id": "zone-orth1", "translation": "girdle"}, {"id": "zone-def1", "translation": "girdle"}, {"id": "zone-quote1", "translation": "from whom she bore the burden of children beneath her girdle"}, {"id": "zone-quote2", "translation": "For how did she nourish you within her girdle, you murderer?"}, {"id": "zone-quote3", "translation": "I have bands and girdles, the fastenings of robes"}, {"id": "zoos-orth1", "translation": "alive"}, {"id": "zoos-def1", "translation": "alive"}, {"id": "zoos-note1", "translation": "in elegy"}, {"id": "zoos-quote1", "translation": "but the fame of the dead is alive"}, {"id": "zopyreo-orth1", "translation": "to kindle"}, {"id": "zopyreo-def1", "translation": "to kindle"}, {"id": "zopyreo-quote1", "translation": "and neighboring cares kindle fear"}, {"id": "zopyreo-quote2", "translation": "of the mind being kindled"}, {"id": "zophytos-orth1", "translation": "life-giving"}, {"id": "zophytos-def1", "translation": "life-giving"}, {"id": "zophytos-quote1", "translation": "from there the life-giving blood, increasing, flourishes for mortals"}]}